GitHub client
-------------

Skeleton only. See PLAN.md in this directory for the full design (GitHub
App registration, OAuth + repo picker, file transfer, webhook sync).

Current state (plan step 2):

- `disconnect`, `write`, `remove` only touch the local blog folder. They
  do not yet talk to the GitHub API.
- `dashboard_routes` exposes a connect page that explains sync is not
  available yet, and a disconnect page.
- `site_routes` exposes `POST /webhook`, which verifies GitHub's
  HMAC-SHA256 signature and responds 200, but does not act on events.
- The client is only registered (`app/clients/index.js`) once all of
  `config.github.{app_id,client_id,client_secret,private_key,
  webhook_secret}` are set, so it stays hidden on the dashboard until a
  real GitHub App exists and its credentials are configured.

Everything else in PLAN.md - OAuth, the repo picker, Redis storage,
transfer, and real commit-backed write/remove - is not implemented yet.
